# Cursor project rules for QS Next.js app

## Project overview
- This workspace is a Next.js 16 app using React 19 and Tailwind CSS.
- The app is organized around the app/ directory for routes and components/ for reusable UI and feature modules.
- The main business domain is project tracking, reporting, and dashboards.

## Development workflow
- Use npm for package management and scripts.
- Run the app with `npm run dev`.
- Build for production with `npm run build`.
- Prefer existing components and utilities over creating new ones when possible.

## Code conventions
- Keep components focused and reusable.
- Use functional React components and hooks.
- Preserve existing project structure unless a change clearly improves it.
- Prefer simple, readable code over clever abstractions.
- Avoid introducing new dependencies unless necessary.

## Important notes
- The project already contains a large set of page and component files; follow existing patterns in nearby files.
- When editing UI, preserve the current styling approach and existing Tailwind classes.
- When working with data and reporting features, keep behavior consistent with the current app patterns.
